                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> I do have a suggestion tho, if it is possible to check if `\"nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects\"` is installed and try to load it after mini ai has been loaded.\r\n\r\nThis is not a good idea for at least these reasons:\r\n- Tree-sitter textobject in 'mini.ai' doesn't *require* 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects'. All they require are reachable queries (i.e. present inside 'runtimepath') for the target language.\r\n- Even if would require queries from 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' specifically, 'mini.ai' doesn't need to do any call (i.e. `require('nvim-treesitter-textobjects')` or else). It only requires properly placed query files which 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' provides just by installing it as any regular plugin.\r\n\r\nOne improvement here might be to detect if there is no query file found for specific language and show that as error when trying to use tree-sitter textobject. I remember looking for something like that initially but found nothing. Now is probably a good time to revisit this.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I do have a suggestion tho, if it is possible to check if <code class=\"notranslate\">\"nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects\"</code> is installed and try to load it after mini ai has been loaded.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is not a good idea for at least these reasons:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Tree-sitter textobject in 'mini.ai' doesn't <em>require</em> 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects'. All they require are reachable queries (i.e. present inside 'runtimepath') for the target language.</li>\n<li>Even if would require queries from 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' specifically, 'mini.ai' doesn't need to do any call (i.e. <code class=\"notranslate\">require('nvim-treesitter-textobjects')</code> or else). It only requires properly placed query files which 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' provides just by installing it as any regular plugin.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One improvement here might be to detect if there is no query file found for specific language and show that as error when trying to use tree-sitter textobject. I remember looking for something like that initially but found nothing. Now is probably a good time to revisit this.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "I do have a suggestion tho, if it is possible to check if \"nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects\" is installed and try to load it after mini ai has been loaded.\n\nThis is not a good idea for at least these reasons:\n\nTree-sitter textobject in 'mini.ai' doesn't require 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects'. All they require are reachable queries (i.e. present inside 'runtimepath') for the target language.\nEven if would require queries from 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' specifically, 'mini.ai' doesn't need to do any call (i.e. require('nvim-treesitter-textobjects') or else). It only requires properly placed query files which 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' provides just by installing it as any regular plugin.\n\nOne improvement here might be to detect if there is no query file found for specific language and show that as error when trying to use tree-sitter textobject. I remember looking for something like that initially but found nothing. Now is probably a good time to revisit this.",
