                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "No worries.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nI've just looked around and [there is already a check for query presence](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4e873f36552ac7c15a824f36783c629493f78d0c/lua/mini/ai.lua#L1514). As there was 'nvim-treesitter' loaded, it didn't trigger (as I couldn't find a way to have the same error for 'nvim-treesitter'). As I have plans to move away from 'nvim-treesitter' as possible dependency, this should resolve by itself soon.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">No worries.</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've just looked around and <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4e873f36552ac7c15a824f36783c629493f78d0c/lua/mini/ai.lua#L1514\">there is already a check for query presence</a>. As there was 'nvim-treesitter' loaded, it didn't trigger (as I couldn't find a way to have the same error for 'nvim-treesitter'). As I have plans to move away from 'nvim-treesitter' as possible dependency, this should resolve by itself soon.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "No worries.\n\nI've just looked around and there is already a check for query presence. As there was 'nvim-treesitter' loaded, it didn't trigger (as I couldn't find a way to have the same error for 'nvim-treesitter'). As I have plans to move away from 'nvim-treesitter' as possible dependency, this should resolve by itself soon.",
